push:"Parents act on push notifications and quick glances. MN parents look several times a day; K12 parents mainly at moments that matter. Either way the phone is the natural device.",
mnLoop:"A short, frequent loop that happens during the school day with a child in the room, so a phone or classroom tablet wins over a desk.",
resultsBoth:"K12 parents want alerts on the phone, but results, học bạ and exam notices are also read, printed or exported; SMAS offers web, app and Excel or PDF export for the same data.",
season:"Seasonal, form-heavy tasks (registration, consent, enrolment) happen once or twice a year, on a phone or at a desk, so support both.",
planning:"Planning and paperwork are long-form desk tasks. Capture observations on the phone and compile plans and records on the web.",
bulk:"Bulk entry, printing and signing with a USB token are desktop tasks, while quick single actions (one score, one period) still suit the phone.",
admin:"Back-office work with many records, filters and bulk actions; the web portal fits. The mobile counterpart is the teacher or parent app.",
leader:"Leaders glance at numbers on the phone and do deeper analysis on the web; MISA ships a mobile leader app for the first part.",
student:"High-school students carry their own phones (a survey cited in a Nghệ An study: 100% of those surveyed, about 5.4 hours a day), so student features must work on mobile; long forms and tests also need a desktop view.",
wallet:"Paying, topping up and checking spend are wallet actions that already live natively in the ECO Me app; accountants reconcile on the web portal.",
live:"Live, time-critical information used on the move (bus position, pick-up), so mobile only for families and drivers; routes are planned on the web."
